WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.930
Content types in Orchard Core have settings that decide where their items appear,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.933
how they are saved, and who can work with them.

00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:14.430
In this video, we'll look at Creatable, Listable, Draftable, Versionable and Securable, and

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.660
at the Stereotype, Category and Thumbnail settings.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:28.274
You find these settings by editing a content type, under Design, Content Definition, Content Types.

00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:33.945
A type you create there starts with Creatable, Listable, Draftable, Versionable and Securable

00:00:33.945 --> 00:00:37.210
all checked, and you clear the ones you don't want.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.565
Creatable offers the type when someone creates an item.

00:00:41.565 --> 00:00:44.460
Listable shows its items in Manage Content.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:50.370
Draftable adds the Save Draft button, and Versionable lets an item keep more than one version.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.722
Securable gives the type its own permissions for roles.

00:00:54.722 --> 00:00:58.205
Stereotype, Category and Thumbnail are text settings:

00:00:58.205 --> 00:01:02.752
a stereotype groups types for a feature, and a category and a thumbnail

00:01:02.752 --> 00:01:04.700
organize types in a picker.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.935
This is Manage Content, and the Event items are listed here.

00:01:12.935 --> 00:01:17.108
The New button offers Event as a type to create, and the Content

00:01:17.108 --> 00:01:19.850
Type filter offers it as a type to list.

00:01:21.485 --> 00:01:23.528
Let's open the settings of Event.

00:01:23.528 --> 00:01:27.353
On the Content Types page, Event has a Create New Event button, and

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.925
Edit opens its settings.

00:01:29.677 --> 00:01:34.666
The form begins with the Technical Name, which can't be changed, and the Display Name.

00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:38.842
Description comes next, and its text appears under the name of the type

00:01:38.842 --> 00:01:40.577
on the Content Types page.

00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:45.448
Each checkbox has a hint next to its label that explains what it does.

00:01:45.448 --> 00:01:47.803
Let's clear Creatable and Listable.

00:01:49.787 --> 00:01:50.819
Choose Save.

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:55.292
Back on Content Types, Event has lost its Create New Event button, while

00:01:55.292 --> 00:01:57.127
List Items is still there.

00:01:57.686 --> 00:02:02.738
On Manage Content, the New button no longer offers Event, the Content Type

00:02:02.738 --> 00:02:06.906
filter no longer lists it, and its items have left the list.

00:02:07.465 --> 00:02:08.994
The items still exist.

00:02:08.994 --> 00:02:13.035
List Items on the Content Types page opens them, because a page that

00:02:13.035 --> 00:02:17.185
asks for one specific type lists it even when the type isn't Listable.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.238
This is the editor of a published Event.

00:02:24.238 --> 00:02:29.347
Publish makes your changes live, and Save Draft stores them without publishing.

00:02:29.347 --> 00:02:33.134
The Save Draft button is here because Event is Draftable.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.801
Let's change the title and choose Save Draft.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:41.310
In Manage Content, the Event shows two badges, Published and Draft.

00:02:41.772 --> 00:02:45.233
The published version stays in place while the draft waits.

00:02:45.233 --> 00:02:47.363
That is what Versionable provides:

00:02:47.363 --> 00:02:49.759
an item can keep more than one version.

00:02:49.759 --> 00:02:52.262
Without it, an item has a single version.

00:02:52.726 --> 00:02:54.817
Let's clear Draftable next.

00:02:54.817 --> 00:02:59.951
On the Edit Content Type page for Event, the Draftable checkbox is checked.

00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:02.106
Uncheck it, and choose Save.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.918
Open another Event.

00:03:03.918 --> 00:03:09.150
Publish is still there, but Save Draft is gone, because the type no longer supports drafts.

00:03:13.436 --> 00:03:17.194
Securable gives a content type permissions of its own.

00:03:17.194 --> 00:03:21.766
To see them, go to Access Control, Roles, and edit the Editor role.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:27.671
Searching the permissions for Event finds a group named Event Content Type - Event.

00:03:27.671 --> 00:03:32.768
It lists permissions such as publish, edit, delete, view, preview and clone for

00:03:32.768 --> 00:03:35.705
Event items, and a permission to list them.

00:03:36.181 --> 00:03:37.948
Let's clear Securable.

00:03:37.948 --> 00:03:43.124
On the Edit Content Type page for Event, uncheck Securable, and choose Save.

00:03:43.124 --> 00:03:46.091
After that, we return to the Editor role.

00:03:46.558 --> 00:03:49.950
Searching the Editor role for Event again finds nothing.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:54.436
Without Securable, the Roles page offers no permissions for the type, so the

00:03:54.436 --> 00:03:58.538
general content permissions decide what a role can do with its items.

00:04:02.793 --> 00:04:06.261
Paragraph is a widget, so its Stereotype is Widget.

00:04:06.261 --> 00:04:11.433
Features that work with widgets offer only the types that have this stereotype.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:16.808
The hint under the Stereotype box gives examples, such as Widget and MenuItem.

00:04:16.808 --> 00:04:21.840
A stereotype of your own is made of letters and digits, and starts with a letter.

00:04:22.371 --> 00:04:26.786
Category groups types in a picker, and Thumbnail is the path of an

00:04:26.786 --> 00:04:28.748
image shown with the type.

00:04:28.748 --> 00:04:34.511
Let's enter Text as the category, a placeholder image as the thumbnail, and choose Save.

00:04:35.027 --> 00:04:37.027
Next, let's create a Page.

00:04:37.027 --> 00:04:41.529
Its editor is set to Blocks, so the plus button, Add Widget, opens

00:04:41.529 --> 00:04:43.717
a picker named Select Widget.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:47.104
The sidebar lists categories, starting with All.

00:04:47.104 --> 00:04:52.103
Text shows only the types of that category, each with its thumbnail and an Add button.

00:04:52.103 --> 00:04:54.710
Types without a category appear under All.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.284
Content type settings decide where items are offered, how they are saved, and

00:05:01.284 --> 00:05:02.881
who can work with them.

00:05:02.881 --> 00:05:07.509
Check the options a type needs, clear the others, and use stereotype, category

00:05:07.509 --> 00:05:09.438
and thumbnail to organize it.

00:05:09.438 --> 00:05:10.870
Thanks for watching.

